\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Causal EEGNet forward pass (read down the left column, then the right). Stacked sheets denote batch $B$; each sheet is drawn at the real extent of its stage, so the height falls from $C=35$ channels to one and the width from $T=2{,}000$ samples to $N=40$ 50-ms bins and finally $(B,N,V)$. Pooling is average ($P=2$, then $Q=25$); dropout is $p=0.25$; all convolutions are causal.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{3}{Causal EEGNet forward pass (read down the left column, then the right). Stacked sheets denote batch $B$; each sheet is drawn at the real extent of its stage, so the height falls from $C=35$ channels to one and the width from $T=2{,}000$ samples to $N=40$ 50-ms bins and finally $(B,N,V)$. Pooling is average ($P=2$, then $Q=25$); dropout is $p=0.25$; all convolutions are causal}{figure.1}{}}
