\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces One causal temporal convolution on a single 1D LFP trial. The input is left-padded with $K_1-1=499$ zeros (grey); the $1\times K_1$ kernel ($K_1=500$ samples, 500~ms) slides left to right. The first output $y[0]$ sees 499 zeros plus $x[0]$; $y[250]$ sees 249 zeros plus $x[0..250]$; after 500 samples the kernel is fully inside the signal. No output sees a future sample. The same left-only scheme is used for the $K_2=62$ separable convolution.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conv}{{3}{7}{One causal temporal convolution on a single 1D LFP trial. The input is left-padded with $K_1-1=499$ zeros (grey); the $1\times K_1$ kernel ($K_1=500$ samples, 500~ms) slides left to right. The first output $y[0]$ sees 499 zeros plus $x[0]$; $y[250]$ sees 249 zeros plus $x[0..250]$; after 500 samples the kernel is fully inside the signal. No output sees a future sample. The same left-only scheme is used for the $K_2=62$ separable convolution}{figure.3}{}}
